<title>UK: Norelf to cease LPG trading.</title>
<headline>Norelf to cease LPG trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norelf Limited, a liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) trading company jointly owned by subsidiaries of Enron Corp and Elf Aquitaine, said on Thursday that it will cease LPG trading effective December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Norelf said in a statement it will maintain its active trading presence until that date. Thereafter, Enron and Elf intend to remain in the international LPG market and to incorporate LPG trading into their respective existing trading operations.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
